  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The most striking finding from the completed experiments is that the multimodal config (config_030: scvi_n200 + ResNet50 + avgpool + concat, acc=0.632) underperforms the RNA-only scvi_n200 configs (config_005: 0.650, config_006: 0.653), and image-only ResNet50 is very weak (0.208). This raises a critical question: is the image modality fundamentally uninformative for this task, or is ResNet50 simply a poor encoder? Config_036 (scvi_n200 + ViT-L + avgpool + concat) changes only the image encoder relative to config_030, cleanly isolating whether a stronger visual representation can contribute complementary signal. If config_036 approaches or exceeds the RNA-only ceiling (~0.653), it validates the multimodal direction and justifies further fusion/aggregation exploration. If it remains at or below RNA-only levels, it strongly indicates the image modality adds no value, allowing us to redirect the remaining budget toward RNA-only refinement (e.g., scvi_n200 with transformer aggregation, or scgpt comparisons). This is the highest-information single-variable experiment available under the budget constraint."
}

